# TLS record buffer sizes, aggressive profile (GD_TLS_BUFFER_PROFILE=2).
#
# Overlay applied on top of sdkconfig.defaults, which is a byte-for-byte copy of the factory
# configuration and is not edited here. Both directions are cut: outgoing records to 2048 bytes,
# incoming records to 8192.
#
# The incoming limit is the risk. A TLS peer may send records of up to 16384 bytes without asking,
# and mbedtls only advertises a smaller limit when the max_fragment_length extension is compiled
# in and the server honours it - neither is the case here. A server that sends a longer record,
# for a certificate chain or a large response body, gets MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_INVALID_RECORD and the
# connection fails. Nothing on the host can tell whether the production backend does; this profile
# is for measurement on hardware against the real server, not for the fleet.
#
# The matching slot geometry is in src/Infrastructure/Adapters/Http/TlsBufferProfile.h. The two
# are checked against each other at compile time, so this file cannot silently fail to arrive.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ASYMMETRIC_CONTENT_LEN=y
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_IN_CONTENT_LEN=8192
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_OUT_CONTENT_LEN=2048
